<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!--
      The window theme, and ONLY the window theme.

      The manifest previously named Theme.Material3.DayNight.NoActionBar, which does
      not exist here: that style ships in the Material COMPONENTS library
      (com.google.android.material), an XML-era dependency this app does not have.
      Compose's material3 artifact provides composables, not XML styles. AAPT was
      right to refuse.

      The fix is not to add that library. This app's UI is entirely Compose, so the
      only thing an XML theme still governs is the window between process start and
      the first frame Compose draws. Pulling in the whole Material Components stack to
      style that moment would add a dependency whose only job is to be unused —
      exactly the kind of weight that accumulates unnoticed.

      So: a platform theme, no dependency. MaterialTheme in MainActivity does the
      actual theming. `android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar` is available from
      API 21 and this app's minSdk is 26, so no version guard is needed.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.SignalGridAssist" parent="android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar" />

</resources>
